{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1848","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Vika and Wiki"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recently, Vika was studying her favorite internet resource - Wikipedia."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the expanses of Wikipedia, she read about an interesting mathematical operation "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", denoted by $$$\\oplus$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vika began to study the properties of this mysterious operation. To do this, she took an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ non-negative integers and applied the following operation to all its elements at the same time: $$$a_i = a_i \\oplus a_{(i+1) \\bmod n}$$$. Here $$$x \\bmod y$$$ denotes the remainder of dividing $$$x$$$ by $$$y$$$. The elements of the array are numbered starting from $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since it is not enough to perform the above actions once for a complete study, Vika repeats them until the array $$$a$$$ becomes all zeros."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine how many of the above actions it will take to make all elements of the array $$$a$$$ zero. If this moment never comes, output $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2^{20}$$$) - the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that $$$n$$$ can be represented as $$$2^k$$$ for some integer $$$k$$$ ($$$0 \\le k \\le 20$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_0, a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_{n-1}$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) - the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single number - the minimum number of actions required to make all elements of the array $$$a$$$ zero, or $$$-1$$$ if the array $$$a$$$ will never become zero."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n1 2 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n0 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n14\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, after one operation, the array $$$a$$$ will become equal to $$$[3, 3, 3, 3]$$$. After one more operation, it will become equal to $$$[0, 0, 0, 0]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, the array $$$a$$$ initially consists only of zeros."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, after one operation, the array $$$a$$$ will become equal to $$$[0]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1848F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1848/problem/F"}